USER ## Key invariants from the doctrine (do not weaken)
USER 
USER - **Roles separate, and the seats are seven:** Owner, Architect, Buyer, Specialist, Maker, Evaluator,
USER   Orchestrator (Playbook §6, Contracts §4). One party may hold several — **recorded as such**. The Owner may
USER   never hold the Evaluator seat on the same job. The Maker never grades its own work.
USER - **The Evaluator recommends; the Orchestrator applies.** Only the Orchestrator applies the pass rule, the
USER   cap, and escalation. An Evaluator that decides whether to iterate has collapsed two roles. Applying
USER   escalation means handing `needs_owner` to the Architect, which writes the options and the recommendation;
USER   the Orchestrator delivers them to the Owner and writes none of it. **Plumbline rule** (Owner ruling
USER   2026-11-04, `schemas/instance-extensions.json` → `escalation_pen`): no doctrine tier names this pen, and
USER   Contracts §4's "recommends … and the Architect decides" is about a design gap, not `needs_owner`.
USER - **Pass rule = `mean >= T_accept` AND `min >= T_dim`.** An average alone lets a fatal defect be averaged
USER   away.
USER - **A verdict needs ≥2 scored runs.** One run is a sample, not a measurement, and a reading resting on one
USER   run is labelled as such (Instrument rule 10).
USER - **Terminal states are exactly `accepted`, `needs_owner`, `rejected`** — and a record carries the **outcome**
USER   it exited under: `accepted` · `census` · `needs_owner` · `rejected` · `no_observation` · `no_artifact`.
USER   An outcome is not a state. Cap-reached above the floor is `needs_owner`, **not** `rejected` — routing it to
USER   `rejected` discards work a human was meant to see.
USER - **`mode: scored` requires a Specialist named at the outset.** With none, the job declares `mode: readings`,
USER   supplies **no thresholds**, returns *conforms / does not conform / unobserved* and **never numbers**, and
USER   **may not produce `rejected`** — there is no floor to be below. Naming a Specialist after the readings are
USER   in does not license scoring.
USER - **A dimension with no observation ⇒ forced `needs_owner`,** never `rejected`, never a synthesised
USER   below-floor score. `observation` is required by the schema, so this is structural.
USER - **A dimension that saw ground truth is invalid.** `saw_gt` fails that dimension (§7.2).
USER - **Entry is decided by the artifact, not by intent.** Work that already exists is Entry B — a labelled
USER   baseline (C32) that is legal only when `reads_before_freeze` names the reads that could reveal a defect and
USER   states they came after the rubric was frozen. A fix is a **new job**.
USER - **Violations are classified into rule 4's four locators** — `artifact_missed_standard`, `standard_moved`,
USER   `dimension_unauthorized`, `frame_at_fault` — never "bad Maker". **There is no severity scale**: `P0/P1/P2`
USER   are undefined and must not be copied or invented. The shortfall is required; the **remedy is optional**,
USER   and a fabricated remedy is itself a violation.
USER - **The instrument is retained with the artifact**, and it is **both** the rubric and the code: the record
USER   names its version and the sha256 of rubric **and** runner (C30). A re-run holding the same rubric and a
USER   different runner is a different instrument.
USER - **A revision carries a control in the same batch.** Comparing against a stored score reports the
USER   instrument's drift as change in the artifact — measured: a document scored 8.64 returned 8.33/8.14/8.00/
USER   7.86/8.39 on byte-identical input.
USER - **Carry the best parts forward.** The standing artifact is the frontier; the **best** artifact is the
USER   Maker's input, with every known defect and its measurement. A trade is the Owner's to declare.
USER - **Verdict and disposition are separate acts.** The Owner may ship a reject or bin an accept; the recorded
USER   verdict stands as the loop produced it.
USER - **External writes are verified by read-back,** with a normalization declared before comparing and a value
USER   fresh on every run (§7.3).
