USER ## Key invariants from the doctrine (do not weaken)
USER 
USER - **Roles separate, and the seats are seven:** Owner, Architect, Buyer, Specialist, Maker, Evaluator,
USER   Orchestrator (Playbook §6, Contracts §4). One party may hold several — **recorded as such**. The Owner may
USER   never hold the Evaluator seat on the same job. The Maker never grades its own work.
USER - **The Evaluator recommends; the Orchestrator applies.** Only the Orchestrator applies the pass rule, the
USER   cap, and escalation. An Evaluator that decides whether to iterate has collapsed two roles. Applying
USER   escalation means handing `needs_owner` to the Architect, which writes the options and the recommendation;
USER   the Orchestrator delivers them to the Owner and writes none of it. **Plumbline rule** (Owner ruling
USER   2026-11-04, `schemas/instance-extensions.json` → `escalation_pen`): no doctrine tier names this pen, and
USER   Contracts §4's "recommends … and the Architect decides" is about a design gap, not `needs_owner`.
USER - **Pass rule = `mean >= T_accept` AND `min >= T_dim`.** An average alone lets a fatal defect be averaged
USER   away.
USER - **A verdict needs ≥2 scored runs.** One run is a sample, not a measurement, and a reading resting on one
USER   run is labelled as such (Instrument rule 10).
USER - **Terminal states are exactly `accepted`, `needs_owner`, `rejected`** — and a record carries the **outcome**
USER   it exited under: `accepted` · `census` · `needs_owner` · `rejected` · `no_observation` · `no_artifact`.
USER   An outcome is not a state. Cap-reached above the floor is `needs_owner`, **not** `rejected` — routing it to
USER   `rejected` discards work a human was meant to see.
USER - **`mode: scored` requires a Specialist named at the outset.** With none, the job declares `mode: readings`,
USER   supplies **no thresholds**, returns *conforms / does not conform / unobserved* and **never numbers**, and
USER   **may not produce `rejected`** — there is no floor to be below. Naming a Specialist after the readings are
USER   in does not license scoring.
USER - **A dimension with no observation ⇒ forced `needs_owner`,** never `rejected`, never a synthesised
USER   below-floor score. `observation` is required by the schema, so this is structural.
USER - **A dimension that saw ground truth is invalid.** `saw_gt` fails that dimension (§7.2).
USER - **Entry is decided by the artifact, not by intent.** Work that already exists is Entry B — a labelled
USER   baseline (C32) that is legal only when `reads_before_freeze` names the reads that could reveal a defect and
USER   states they came after the rubric was frozen. A fix is a **new job**.
USER - **Violations are classified into rule 4's four locators** — `artifact_missed_standard`, `standard_moved`,
USER   `dimension_unauthorized`, `frame_at_fault` — never "bad Maker". **There is no severity scale**: `P0/P1/P2`
USER   are undefined and must not be copied or invented. The shortfall is required; the **remedy is optional**,
USER   and a fabricated remedy is itself a violation.
USER - **The instrument is retained with the artifact**, and it is **both** the rubric and the code: the record
USER   names its version and the sha256 of rubric **and** runner (C30). A re-run holding the same rubric and a
USER   different runner is a different instrument.
USER - **A revision carries a control in the same batch.** Comparing against a stored score reports the
USER   instrument's drift as change in the artifact — measured: a document scored 8.64 returned 8.33/8.14/8.00/
USER   7.86/8.39 on byte-identical input.
USER - **Carry the best parts forward.** The standing artifact is the frontier; the **best** artifact is the
USER   Maker's input, with every known defect and its measurement. A trade is the Owner's to declare.
USER - **Verdict and disposition are separate acts.** The Owner may ship a reject or bin an accept; the recorded
USER   verdict stands as the loop produced it.
USER - **External writes are verified by read-back,** with a normalization declared before comparing and a value
USER   fresh on every run (§7.3).
USER 
USER ## The instance layer (Contracts §8 / C18 — labelled, and it weakens nothing)
USER 
USER Declared in `schemas/instance-extensions.json`. Each item is Plumbline's, not the doctrine's:
USER 
USER - **The standing constitution** (`constitution.schema.json`) — the Owner's values, principles and escalation
USER   classes for one program, each value carrying a `decision_rule` so it can arbitrate. **Subordinate to the
USER   mandate:** the mandate is the doctrine's frame instrument; the constitution is this instance's encoding of
USER   it. A disagreement escalates to the Owner and is never auto-resolved.
USER - **`stage`** — the chain-of-loops label, **optional**, and **the decision is DEFERRED, not open**.
USER   `constitution.schema.json` declares `principles[].applies_to_stages`, so a stage-scoped principle would be
USER   evaluated *using the packet's stage* — but **the ratified constitution carries no stage-scoped principle**:
USER   of its seven principles exactly one declares `applies_to_stages`, and it declares it empty (`[]` — the whole
USER   chain, not a stage), so nothing is scoped to a stage and the trigger never fires. *(Corrected 2026-10-01:
USER   the earlier reason — "no constitution instance exists anywhere" — stopped being true when
USER   `dot-plumbline/constitution.json` was ratified. The deferral is unchanged; its stated reason was not.)* Requiring the field (or writing the stage → ground-truth/channel map
USER   as law) would be a check that cannot fail, which Instrument rule 3 bars.
USER   **Revisit when either:** (i) a constitution instance carries a stage-scoped principle; (ii) a conductor runs
USER   a real job whose ground-truth channel needs classifying.
USER - **What `stage` does *not* do:** carry the elicitation rule. A job with no independent ground truth cannot
USER   be scored whatever its label, because C33 requires non-empty `ground_truth`, `mandate_ref` and `escalation` on
USER   a scored job and an unratified job can never reach `accepted`. The field **classifies**; it does not gate.
USER - **The stage → ground-truth/evidence-channel map** lives only in prose (GOALS.md's Stage Map) and is law
USER   nowhere: the packet records its own `ground_truth[]` and nothing checks the row against the stage. That is a
USER   deliberate deferral, not an oversight — see above.
USER - **The discoverability gate** — before any escalation, classify: *discoverable* (search, measurement, reading
USER   the repo, probing the record, running the code) → resolve it and never ask; *undecidable* (values, doctrine,
USER   Buyer intent, priority, risk appetite) → escalate, carrying the question, what was tried, why no observable
USER   answer exists, **and the options with a recommendation** — written by the Architect, delivered by the
USER   Orchestrator (Plumbline rule: `escalation_pen`). An escalation without options is work pushed back.
USER   Metric: **discoverable-escalation rate**.
USER - **Seat entitlement** (Owner ruling 2026-11-06, every E-DI loop). Every seat must be provided everything it is entitled to for making its best contribution to the job — and nothing more. The list: clear instructions, essential context, necessary computing resources, appropriate tooling, adequate tokens, ample time, and the full scope of agency vested in that seat. Entitlement is the ceiling as well as the floor. Do not hand a seat another seat's material, another seat's agency, held-out, or a diagnosis it was not vested to make. The Orchestrator owns delivering this, and owns not delivering past it. The information bound is Contracts §4.2, C39: findings reach the Maker and the Architect with every known defect and its measurement, and only held-out material is withheld. Tokens, time, and tooling are the packet's bounds, not C39. Architect: the failure record of the job, the tree, the bars, the packet, the doctrine pin. Maker: the red, rule 12, and an editable set that includes the file the bar fails in. Evaluator: the frozen standard and the turn — never held-out material, never the Maker's model. Entitlement is the record and the paths, not the Orchestrator's diagnosis of the fix. A brief made short rather than complete is a choke; the seat answers honestly against a partial surface and the answer is useless.
USER - **Two dimensions the Contracts cannot supply** — *operator burden* and *proportionality*. Three of the
USER   direction's four falsification conditions cannot be contract violations, so a contract-derived evaluator is
USER   blind to them. **Operator burden is DEFINED as operator FRICTION** (2026-10-05, Owner instruction): zero weight
USER   on his ratifications, selections and amendments — architecture is a collaborative stage and his judgement there
USER   is designed-in — and weight only on what the loop took from him: a reading he had to ask about, a question
USER   asked twice, a re-ratification caused by a defect of ours. **Target zero, counted absolutely per job; never a
USER   ratio against engagement**, because that denominator lets the program that imposed more unnecessary work read
USER   better. Design rule: the metric must never be improvable by showing him less of the work. Declared in
USER   `schemas/instance-extensions.json` → `operator_friction`; first reading 1 event across 5 jobs.
USER - **The Maker carries task classes** (generation ≠ revision, each shown by a completed run). Doctrine requires
USER   this (§4.1, rule 10); C33 does not enforce it structurally, so Plumbline does.
USER - **The standing authorization** (`standing_authorization` in `schemas/instance-extensions.json`) — the Owner's
USER   risk appetite for **ordinary operating actions**, authorized 2026-09-30. Read the two lists **there**; do not
USER   restate them here, because a restatement is a second place to go stale. It came from measurement rather than
USER   preference: `tools/measure_operator_burden.py` found **236 repeated same-shape approval asks in 30 days**,
USER   while the Owner's two other operator-burden signals sat at zero. The defect was asking per *instance* about a
USER   shape already settled, so the three authorized shapes stop being questions and the rest keep asking.
