USER ## Profile roster
USER 
USER **The Evaluator seat is built and has run a job.** `plumbline-eval` — model `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` via provider
USER `openrouter`, a **different model family** from the Maker (DeepSeek), per rule 2. Smoke-tested before the job.
USER 
USER - **THE `base_url` TRAP, on every new seat.** A new profile inherits `model.base_url` from `default`. With
USER   `model.provider: openrouter` and an inherited `base_url: https://api.deepseek.com/v1`, GLM requests would
USER   have been routed to **DeepSeek's own server** — role separation nominally satisfied and actually violated,
USER   because the "independent" evaluator would have run on the maker's infrastructure. Clear `model.base_url`
USER   when pinning a seat, and verify the seat answers before building anything on it.
USER - **The seat is a heavy reasoner.** ~6.5k reasoning tokens per clause plus the surface, so 33 clauses in one
USER   call needs ~200k and never completes (`finish_reason: length`, empty content). Chunk the clauses; bound
USER   thinking with `reasoning: {max_tokens: N}`.
USER 
USER The remaining seats are unbuilt. The seat set is Playbook §6's seven; these are the profiles that would carry
USER them (one profile per role, model pinned per profile — the §4 role-independence mechanism).
USER 
USER | Profile | Seat | Tools | Notes |
USER |---|---|---|---|
USER | `<program>-conductor` | Orchestrator | none | Routes, enforces bounds, applies the pass rule, runs the discoverability gate; hands `needs_owner` to the Architect and delivers its options. Decides nothing. |
USER | `<program>-maker` | Maker | file, terminal (write) | Works in a git worktree |
USER | `<program>-eval` | Evaluator | file, terminal (read/run) | **Different model family** from the Maker. No write tools. |
USER | `<program>-deploy` | Deployment | terminal, web | Read-back verification scripts |
USER | `<program>-audit` | Auditor | file, terminal | Job-record audit + discoverable-escalation rate |
USER 
USER **Constraint:** `delegate_task` children all inherit one model from `delegation.*` config — there is no
USER per-child model. Role separation therefore requires separate profiles/processes, not subagents. This also
USER preserves prompt caching.
