USER 
USER A harness log is what tools/edi/or_call.py appends (its append_entry): one entry
USER per model call, each carrying `call`, `sent_at`, `received_at` (RFC 3339 UTC),
USER the `request` url and the `response` model. The file is a JSON list; a file that
USER holds a single entry object is accepted too.
USER 
USER The emitter asks this module one thing of the log: is it sound, and for a named
USER call, when did it start and end, and where does that time come from? A malformed,
USER partial or reversed log raises HarnessLogError naming the entry, so the emitter
USER can REFUSE the record rather than take a check time from a log it cannot honestly
USER read.
USER """
